  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 8,
  "Question": "In a certain year the price of gasoline rose by \\(20\\%\\) during January, fell by \\(20\\%\\) during February, rose by \\(25\\%\\) during March, and fell by \\(x\\%\\) during April. The price of gasoline at the end of April was the same as it had been at the beginning of January. To the nearest integer, what is \\(x?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(12\\)",
    "B": "\\(17\\)",
    "C": "\\(20\\)",
    "D": "\\(25\\)",
    "E": "\\(35\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Measure prices in units that make the initial price \\(100\\). This rescales every price equally and preserves all percentage changes.\n\nAfter January the price is \\(100(1.20)=120\\). After February it is \\(120(0.80)=96\\), and after March it is \\(96(1.25)=120\\).\n\nApril must therefore reduce the price from \\(120\\) to \\(100\\). The decrease is \\(20\\), and its percentage must be measured relative to April's starting price of \\(120\\):\n\\[\nx=\\frac{20}{120}\\cdot100\n=\\frac{50}{3}\n=16\\frac23.\n\\]\nTo the nearest integer, \\(x=\\boxed{17}\\), choice B.",
